samples.evidence:
The new report helper builds the absence census line inline:

```js
const absent = l.census?.[key]?.absent ?? {};
const declared = LATENCY_ABSENT.map((f) => `${f}=${absent[f] ?? 0}`);
const extra = Object.keys(absent).filter((f) => !LATENCY_ABSENT.includes(f)).map((f) => `UNRECOGNISED ${f}=${absent[f]}`);
```

This is character-for-character the body of `latencyAbsentLine` in `scripts/agent/eval/adapters/coderabbit.mjs:1200-1205`, which the arm adapter exports *specifically* so the wording is shared and testable ("Exported for the same reason `latencyLine` is, and it has already earned it… the wording matches so the two reports read alike", coderabbit.mjs:1186-1199; also recorded in docs/tasks/active/20260812-coderabbit-latency-todo.md:134-139, where the formatter was extracted and exported *in review* for exactly this reason). The diff even imports `LATENCY_ABSENT` from that module while skipping the function built on it, so the two copies can now drift (a future change to the unrecognised-row wording, or to the declared-order rule, only lands in one report). This is the reuse expectation the same import block claims to be honouring for `SELF_TIMED_INTERVAL`/`PUSH_PROXY_INTERVAL`/`latencyCensus`.

